{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce.</b> Even at the time of reproof, he cursed only their anger — and this is what Balaam said: ״מָה אֶקֹּב לֹא קַבֹּה אֵל״ (Numbers 23)." "<b>I will divide them in Jacob.</b> I will separate them one from the other, so that Levi has no portion among the tribes — and see, they are divided. Another interpretation: you find poor men and scribes and teachers of children only from Simeon, so that they are scattered; and the tribe of Levi He made go around to the granaries for terumot and tithes — He gave him his dispersion by way of honor."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:02.443904197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}